WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.672 --> 00:00:14.096
Three days and three nights had gone by since the train had left San Francisco.

2
00:00:15.376 --> 00:00:20.638
The travelers had passed the Great Salt Lake in Utah, traveled over the Rocky Mountains, and crossed the

3
00:00:20.678 --> 00:00:21.738
prairies of Wyoming.

4
00:00:22.938 --> 00:00:27.559
In Nebraska they had reached the Platte River, which the rail line was now following, 350 miles before

5
00:00:27.579 --> 00:00:33.406
Omaha. Four more days and nights remained until they would reach New York.

6
00:00:34.307 --> 00:00:36.029
Phileas Fogg was right on schedule.

7
00:00:36.909 --> 00:00:41.493
Mr. Fogg and his friends continued their whist game, and no one complained about the length of the

8
00:00:41.533 --> 00:00:47.518
trip. During the morning Fix had won several guineas, which he now seemed likely to lose.

9
00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.241
The train pulled into the station at Plum Creek.

10
00:00:52.342 --> 00:00:57.186
Mr. Fogg was about to play a winning spade when a voice from behind him said, "A smart

11
00:00:57.226 --> 00:00:58.908
whist player would play a diamond!"

12
00:00:59.784 --> 00:01:00.924
It was Colonel Proctor.

13
00:01:00.944 --> 00:01:04.645
"I see I have found you, Englishman," said the colonel.

14
00:01:06.246 --> 00:01:07.286
Aouda turned pale.

15
00:01:07.946 --> 00:01:08.747
She seized Mr.

16
00:01:08.787 --> 00:01:09.407
Fogg's arm.

17
00:01:10.107 --> 00:01:10.707
But it was Mr.

18
00:01:10.807 --> 00:01:14.468
Fix who stood up and said, "Pardon me, but this is my affair.

19
00:01:15.449 --> 00:01:19.950
You hit me, Colonel, and now you are being insolent with one of my friends.

20
00:01:20.870 --> 00:01:22.250
I will challenge you myself!"

21
00:01:23.691 --> 00:01:25.771
"Mr. Fix, you will not," said Mr.

22
00:01:25.811 --> 00:01:27.192
Fogg, rising from his seat.

23
00:01:28.172 --> 00:01:32.735
"The colonel has insulted me a second time by suggesting that I play a diamond.

24
00:01:33.615 --> 00:01:35.856
I have no more patience for this rude American.

25
00:01:36.797 --> 00:01:38.578
I challenge you to a duel, Colonel!"

26
00:01:38.598 --> 00:01:44.421
"I accept your challenge," replied Colonel Proctor, "with whatever weapon you choose!"

27
00:01:45.962 --> 00:01:47.463
Passepartout wanted to beg Mr.

28
00:01:47.503 --> 00:01:51.725
Fogg not to proceed but knew that, as Fogg's servant, he must hold his tongue.

29
00:01:52.566 --> 00:01:54.687
Aouda, on the other hand, pleaded with Mr.

30
00:01:54.727 --> 00:01:56.128
Fogg not to risk his life.

31
00:01:56.916 --> 00:02:02.459
Mr. Fogg calmly selected four revolvers from Passepartout's collection and handed two to the colonel.

32
00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:06.962
He left the car, and the American followed him out onto the platform.

33
00:02:08.103 --> 00:02:11.645
The weather had turned cold and scattered snowflakes were drifting in the air.

34
00:02:12.485 --> 00:02:16.107
The conductor hurried to them to say the train was about to get underway again.

35
00:02:16.127 --> 00:02:18.889
"We are already twenty minutes late, gentlemen.

36
00:02:19.429 --> 00:02:21.270
Please board the train," he said.

37
00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:24.052
"We mean to fight a duel!

38
00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.621
And we would like to do it here and now," said Mr.

39
00:02:27.661 --> 00:02:31.003
Fogg. "I'm really very sorry," said the conductor.

40
00:02:31.023 --> 00:02:36.045
"Under any other circumstances, I'd be willing to oblige you, but there is no time.

41
00:02:36.786 --> 00:02:38.707
Why not fight as we go along?"

42
00:02:40.047 --> 00:02:41.428
The men reboarded the train.

43
00:02:42.688 --> 00:02:45.930
As it left the station, they followed the conductor to the last car.

44
00:02:47.211 --> 00:02:49.692
The conductor quickly relocated its few passengers.

45
00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:56.805
Mr. Fogg and Colonel Proctor, each carrying two six-barreled revolvers, faced each other at opposite ends of the

46
00:02:56.845 --> 00:02:57.405
empty car.

47
00:02:58.586 --> 00:03:00.788
They agreed to begin firing on the count of three.

48
00:03:02.669 --> 00:03:06.352
Fix and Passepartout, their hearts beating, waited outside the door.

49
00:03:07.093 --> 00:03:12.277
Suddenly they heard savage cries, accompanied by gunshots, but the shots did not come from the last car

50
00:03:12.297 --> 00:03:12.797
of the train.

51
00:03:14.518 --> 00:03:16.600
Shrieks of terror came from the passengers.

52
00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.421
Colonel Proctor and Mr.

53
00:03:19.441 --> 00:03:24.944
Fogg, revolvers in hand, left their dueling car and rushed to the forward cars with Fix and Passepartout.

54
00:03:26.205 --> 00:03:28.326
They saw right away what was causing the commotion.

55
00:03:31.148 --> 00:03:34.409
A hundred Indians had leaped from galloping horses onto the train.

56
00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:39.372
Three had climbed onto the engine and knocked the engineer unconscious.

57
00:03:40.233 --> 00:03:43.134
Now the train was racing forward at an uncontrollable speed.

58
00:03:43.955 --> 00:03:45.416
The Indians were armed with guns.

59
00:03:46.348 --> 00:03:49.570
They slipped through the windows and doors of the cars, shooting at the passengers.

60
00:03:50.971 --> 00:03:53.213
Many passengers were armed as well and fired back.

61
00:03:55.574 --> 00:03:57.215
The conductor was fighting beside Mr.

62
00:03:57.255 --> 00:04:02.739
Fogg. He knew that a garrison of soldiers was at the next station, Fort Kearney, which they were

63
00:04:02.779 --> 00:04:03.540
fast approaching.

64
00:04:04.721 --> 00:04:08.303
Their only hope was to stop the train so that the soldiers could come to their aid.

65
00:04:09.344 --> 00:04:11.045
A shot hit the conductor in the chest.

66
00:04:12.586 --> 00:04:16.693
As he fell, he cried, "Unless the train is stopped, we are lost!"

67
00:04:19.234 --> 00:04:23.557
"It shall be stopped," said Phileas Fogg, preparing to rush through the cars to the engine.

68
00:04:23.577 --> 00:04:27.300
"Stay, monsieur, and protect Aouda," said Passepartout.

69
00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:28.460
"I will go!"

70
00:04:29.541 --> 00:04:34.144
Mr. Fogg had no time to stop the courageous Passepartout, who crawled through a door and slipped under

71
00:04:34.184 --> 00:04:34.625
the train!

72
00:04:37.647 --> 00:04:44.551
While bullets whizzed between the Indians and the passengers, smashing windows and puncturing seats, Passepartout clung dangerously above

73
00:04:44.571 --> 00:04:45.432
the speeding tracks.

74
00:04:46.668 --> 00:04:50.311
He crawled forward from one car to the next until he reached the first car.

75
00:04:51.672 --> 00:04:56.016
Hanging by one hand, he released the chains that attached the engine to the rest of the train.

76
00:04:58.297 --> 00:05:01.900
The train shuddered violently, and the engine detached from the rest of the cars.

77
00:05:03.662 --> 00:05:06.264
The engine raced ahead, but the cars began to slow.

78
00:05:07.825 --> 00:05:11.088
After several minutes they stopped, only a hundred feet from the station.

79
00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:16.032
Passepartout crawled out from underneath the first car.

80
00:05:17.004 --> 00:05:20.045
Before he could brush himself off, he felt a pistol against his head.

81
00:05:21.186 --> 00:05:25.768
He turned to see a group of Indians had surrounded him on horseback, and everything went black.

82
00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:30.770
Help! Help!

83
00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:31.991
Somebody, help me!

84
00:05:32.971 --> 00:05:33.551
Oh, hello there.

85
00:05:34.012 --> 00:05:36.933
As you can see, I'm in a bit of trouble, captured by Indians!

86
00:05:37.733 --> 00:05:38.333
Let's hope Mr.

87
00:05:38.353 --> 00:05:39.814
Fogg comes to my rescue soon.

88
00:05:40.734 --> 00:05:42.195
At least he didn't get killed in that duel.

89
00:05:43.216 --> 00:05:43.996
What was he thinking?

90
00:05:45.292 --> 00:05:49.254
Perhaps you have realized this on your own, but a duel is a confrontation between two men.

91
00:05:50.255 --> 00:05:54.117
A duel is usually arranged when one man is insulted or wronged by the other man.

92
00:05:54.978 --> 00:05:55.798
For example, Mr.

93
00:05:55.838 --> 00:06:00.261
Fogg said that Colonel Proctor had insulted him twice, so he challenged Proctor to a duel.

94
00:06:00.941 --> 00:06:02.682
It was a way of regaining his honor.

95
00:06:04.203 --> 00:06:07.785
Duels are usually fought with guns and are common in Europe and the United States.

96
00:06:08.625 --> 00:06:12.928
They frequently take place at dawn so the men will not be interrupted by townspeople or police.

97
00:06:14.380 --> 00:06:19.742
Duels are also common among cowboys in the "Wild West" of America, especially when a new cowboy comes

98
00:06:19.782 --> 00:06:20.222
to town.

99
00:06:21.743 --> 00:06:26.645
For a duel with guns, two men stand back-to-back, and then walk forward a certain number of steps.

100
00:06:27.705 --> 00:06:30.546
After that, they quickly turn to face each other and shoot.

101
00:06:31.707 --> 00:06:33.347
It's a dangerous way to settle an argument!
